<profiles>
<profile name="Krushin&apos; Impetus" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities" hidden="false" id="0d1a-e10f-0016">
<characteristics>
<characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">When this unit ends a **charge move**, you can select one enemy unit **engaged** with this unit. If you do, roll one D6 for each model in this unit **engaged** with that enemy unit:
- For each 3+, that enemy unit suffers 1 **mortal wound**.</characteristic>
</characteristics>
</profile>
<profile name="Intimidating Motivation" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities" hidden="false" id="0d1a-e10f-0017">
<characteristics>
<characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">**Once per battle round, per army.** In your Movement phase, at the start or end of this unit&apos;s move, you can select one friendly **^^Orks^^** unit within 6&quot; of this unit. That unit:
- Is no longer **battle-shocked**.
- Is **riled up** until the start of your next turn.</characteristic>
</characteristics>
</profile>
</profiles>
